A class chart shows four living things with their habitat and one feature:
camel - hot desert of Rajasthan - long legs with wide hooves;
deodar - snowy Himalayas of Himachal Pradesh - conical shape with sloping branches;
sea fish - ocean - streamlined body;
rhododendron - windy mountaintops of the Nilgiris - short, with small leaves.
(i) Group the four habitats as terrestrial or aquatic.
(ii) For the camel and the fish, say which condition of the habitat the feature helps with.
(iii) Which two features help with moving about, and which two help a plant deal with the weather?
(iv) The hot desert and the deodar's mountains both get cold. How do their cold conditions differ, and which feature in the chart deals with cold?
(v) Use your answers to explain why the plants and animals of the ocean differ from those of the desert.
